---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Container from '../../components/Container.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import TranslationNotice from '../../components/TranslationNotice.astro';

/* Английская редакция `/consent`, построена 2026-08-26. Источник содержания
 * — `docs/legal/public/consent.md`, редакция 1.3 от 2026-08-25, та же
 * редакция и дата, что у русской страницы `/consent`. Оговорка о приоритете
 * (`TranslationNotice`) — сразу после заголовка. Форма ссылается сюда с
 * `/en` (`LeadForm.astro`, `locale === 'en'`). */
---
<Base title="Consent to the Processing of Personal Data — wfeels"
      description="Consent to the processing of data submitted through the wfeels.site form."
      noindex={true}>
  <Container>
    <Section>
      <h1 class="t-h1">Consent to the Processing of Personal Data</h1>
      <TranslationNotice ruHref="/consent" />
      <Prose>
        <p><strong>Revision 1.3 of 25 August 2026.</strong></p>
        <p>
          Status: the edition in force for the mandatory, not
          pre-ticked, form checkbox. It is not combined with accepting the
          Terms, a marketing mailing list, or permission to publish a case
          study.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who this consent is given to</h2>
        <p>
          I give my consent to Сабуров Даниил Денисович, Tax ID 183700967882,
          a self-employed individual under the
          Professional Income Tax regime, place of business — Saint
          Petersburg, email <code>i@dsaburov.ru</code>, to process my
          personal data on the terms below.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Purposes</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>to receive and review my enquiry;</li>
          <li>to contact me by the method I specified;</li>
          <li>to clarify the task, timeline and an estimate of cost;</li>
          <li>to prepare a proposal, a specification and an individual contract at my initiative;</li>
          <li>to confirm the fact and the terms of this consent.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This consent does not permit marketing mailings, mass messages,
          or publication of my name, testimonial or project materials.
        </p>
        <p>
          A Telegram username may be given as a contact for a reply. Direct
          correspondence that a user starts themselves via a Telegram link
          is also governed by the terms of that service, and is not a
          submission of the web form.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Data covered</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>name or preferred form of address;</li>
          <li>the email or Telegram username I provide;</li>
          <li>the selected service;</li>
          <li>a description of the task;</li>
          <li>the date and time of submission, the page URL, and the enquiry identifier;</li>
          <li>the version of the Policy and of this consent, and the fact and method of confirmation;</li>
          <li>my reply to a follow-up question, if sent through the same verified channel and relating to this enquiry.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Limited technical data used for site security is processed
          separately, on the basis stated in the Privacy Policy, not on the
          basis of this checkbox. Once negotiations begin, business
          correspondence may be processed to conclude a contract at my
          initiative; this is also a separate basis.
        </p>
        <p>
          I understand that the free-text field is not meant for passport
          or banking details, special-category or biometric data, or
          personal data of third parties. I will not enter such information
          unless it is genuinely necessary and an agreed secure channel has
          been set up.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Operations and method</h2>
        <p>
          Collection, recording, systematisation, accumulation, storage,
          clarification, retrieval, use, transfer to a party lawfully
          entrusted with processing, blocking, deletion and destruction are
          permitted. Processing is carried out by automated and mixed
          means.
        </p>
        <p>
          The primary SQLite database is on a RUVDS VPS in the RUcloud data
          centre at: Russian Federation, Moscow Region, Korolyov,
          Pionerskaya St., 4. Only after the record has been successfully
          written there is a full copy of the enquiry sent via the Telegram
          Bot API to the Controller's private service chat. Telegram uses
          foreign distributed infrastructure and group entities across
          several jurisdictions. I have been informed of the cross-border
          nature of this delivery and I consent to it, for the stated
          purposes and to the stated extent. The bot deletes the Telegram
          copy after 23 hours, and the private chat's own «1 day»
          auto-delete timer serves as an independent safeguard; the standard
          retention period does not exceed 24 hours.
        </p>
        <p>
          VPS infrastructure is provided by OOO «МТ ФИНАНС» (trading as
          RUVDS), Tax ID <code>7706424050</code>, OGRN{' '}
          <code>1157746680332</code>, registered address: 127051, Moscow,
          Tsvetnoy Blvd, 26, bldg. 1, room 12. This is a provider of leased
          computing infrastructure; the application and the enquiry
          database are administered by the Controller. Access to the
          application and database is restricted by technical means and the
          Controller's own credentials.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Duration</h2>
        <p>
          This consent is valid until its purposes are achieved, but an
          enquiry that does not result in a contract is kept for no more
          than 90 calendar days from submission. Limited evidence of
          consent may be kept for no more than 1095 calendar days from
          submission, to prove its lawfulness.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a contract is concluded, the data needed for the contract,
          payments, acceptance of work, compliance with the law, and
          defence of rights continues to be processed on the corresponding
          lawful bases, for the periods set out in the Privacy Policy.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Withdrawal and rights</h2>
        <p>
          Consent can be withdrawn by writing to{' '}
          <a href="mailto:i@dsaburov.ru">i@dsaburov.ru</a> with the subject
          line «Отзыв согласия на обработку персональных данных» (Withdrawal
          of consent to the processing of personal data). The message
          should state the contact used in the enquiry and details that
          allow it to be found without collecting extra data.
        </p>
        <p>
          On receiving a withdrawal, the Controller stops processing and
          destroys the data no later than 30 calendar days afterwards,
          unless another lawful basis exists. If part of the data continues
          to be processed on another basis, the Controller states the
          scope, purpose, basis and duration of that processing in the
          reply to the subject.
        </p>
        <p>
          Full details are set out in the{' '}
          <a href="/en/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Wording used on the form</h2>
        <p>The checkbox is empty by default. The text next to it reads:</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            I give consent to the processing of my data (name, contact
            details, selected service, enquiry text) so you can reply to my
            enquiry, including delivery of a copy through Telegram.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          The words «consent to the processing of my data» link to{' '}
          <a href="/en/consent">/en/consent</a>. In the same visual block, but
          outside the checkbox's own label, sits the line «For details, see
          the privacy policy», linking to{' '}
          <a href="/en/privacy">/en/privacy</a>. The Privacy Policy is not
          «accepted» by this checkbox. The server stores the revisions of
          both documents, the time, the enquiry identifier, the exact
          wording of the action, and the fact that the checkbox was ticked.
        </p>
      </Prose>
      <a href="/en#contact" class="back-to-form">
        <span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to the form
      </a>
    </Section>
  </Container>
</Base>
